<%#
  The City pill in a screen's header, and the picker it opens. With one city
  there is nothing to pick, so it is only a label. With more, it is a
  <details>: the pill is its summary, and the cities drop below it as
  buttons. The choice is kept per person, so picking is a post that lands
  back on `back`.

  It lives in a header, which sits outside every form on these screens, so
  the menu can be a form of its own. The new-watch form picks its City
  inside itself instead, and does not draw this.
%>
<% if city_switch? %>
  <details class="city-picker">
    <summary class="pill pill--small city-picker__pill" aria-label="City: <%= h(current_city) %>. Change"><%= icon(:pin, size: 14) %><%= h(current_city) %><%= icon(:chevron, size: 14) %></summary>
    <form class="city-picker__menu" method="post" action="/city" aria-label="City">
      <input type="hidden" name="back" value="<%= h(back) %>">
      <% cities.each do |city| %>
        <button class="city-picker__option" name="city" value="<%= h(city) %>"<%= ' aria-current="true"' if city == current_city %>><span><%= h(city) %></span><%= icon(:check, size: 16) if city == current_city %></button>
      <% end %>
    </form>
  </details>
<% else %>
  <span class="pill pill--small"><%= icon(:pin, size: 14) %><%= h(current_city) %></span>
<% end %>
